{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 21, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "**Cherry Blossoms and Neon Lights: My Japan Adventure**\n\nStepping off the plane in Tokyo, I was immediately struck by the perfect blend of ancient tradition and futuristic innovation. My two-week journey through Japan was nothing short of magical.\n\nI started in Kyoto, where the air smelled of incense and pine. Walking through the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove felt like entering another world, with towering green stalks swaying gently overhead. The highlight was undoubtedly Fushimi Inari Taisha. Hiking up the thousands of vibrant vermilion torii gates offered a serene escape from the crowds below.\n\nA high-speed Shinkansen ride later, I arrived in the electric heart of Tokyo. Shibuya Crossing was a chaotic dance of humanity, yet everything moved with rhythmic precision. By day, I explored the quiet, narrow alleys of Asakusa, visiting the historic Senso-ji Temple. By night, the city transformed into a neon wonderland. I savored fresh sushi at the Tsukiji Outer Market and warmed up with a steaming bowl of ramen in a tiny alleyway stall.\n\nThe kindness of the locals was unmatched. Whether it was a shopkeeper bowing deeply or a stranger going out of their way to give directions, the hospitality made me feel welcome.\n\nJapan is a place where you can find silence in a bustling city and excitement in a quiet village. From the delicate beauty of cherry blossoms to the hum of a bullet train, every moment was a discovery. I left with a full camera roll and an even fuller heart, already dreaming of my next return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.29092026}, {"token": "Ch", "logprob": -0.41426665}, {"token": "erry", "logprob": -0.25197315}, {"token": " Bloss", "logprob": -0.001376861}, {"token": "oms", "logprob": -9.536748e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -5.6864446e-05}, {"token": " Neon", "logprob": -0.12565766}, {"token": " Lights", "logprob": -0.071